WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:09.010
<i>A mushroom warning has been issued.</i>

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:16.370
<i>Please take precautions
 to avoid inhaling spores.</i>

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.640
Whoa, it's huge.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.750
What <i>is</i> that?

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.600
You ever seen anything that big before?

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.120
Nope.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.130
Maybe I should get another job.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.660
Hey, come on, girls, get inside. 
What if you inhale spores?

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.130
Coming.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.130
Bad news!

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.530
The doctor's...

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.010
Panda Clinic's been hit by a terrorist attack!

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:39.890
What did you say?!

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.390
What about Doctor Nekoyanagi?
He's safe, right?

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.720
We don't know yet...

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.390
There you are!

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.520
What are you doing over here?

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.950
Oh, it's you guys. H-Have you 
actually been searching for him?

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.740
He's causing havoc over at the West Gate.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:58.020
Is that so? Let's leave him to whoever's 
in charge at the West Gate, then.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.320
Come on, let's go.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.280
Huh? No, I was only told to search downtown...

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.020
Whoa!

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.960
W-Wait! Don't touch me there!

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.260
<b>Tag Team</b>

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.390
W-Wait! Just hold on a second!

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.560
I-I was against this!

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.010
I told them such a kind man 
could never be a villain, right?

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.520
Yet that governor forced me to do this!

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:10.550
Hey. Who in the hell are you people?
What happened to the Watch?

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:15.620
H-Hey, killing such an innocent girl 
would just haunt your dreams, right?

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:20.620
I-I'm quitting this line of work today, 
so I could even give you the job—

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.080
Scary.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.940
He's scary.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.690
m 0 0 s 100 0 100 100 0 100 c

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.690
Emergency
\h\h\h\h\hUse

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.690
<b>Artificial
\h\h\h\hBlood</b>

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.690
m 0 0 l 100 4 100 100 0 100

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.690
<b>Keep Preserved</b>

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.250
This artificial blood 
should be compatible.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.740
What an awful case of Rusting.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.140
At this point, even if his injuries heal...

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.780
I only... have about a month left.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.660
Huh? You're already conscious?

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.460
Oh, I'm doing a blood transfusion, 
so don't move.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:02.210
I didn't know your blood type, 
but luckily, it's compatible.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.380
Blood type?

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.620
What's that?

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.860
Hey, I said don't move!

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.940
So are you a doctor?

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.360
What happened to those punks?

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:18.870
Akaboshi-san's drawing their attention
 away by causing chaos outside.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.880
You're pretty skilled despite your age.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.570
Ow.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.850
Guess I shouldn't move yet.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.950
Um, who are you, exactly?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.340
How do you know Akaboshi-san?

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.970
I'm Jabi.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:38.370
I'm Bisco's...

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.390
Well, I guess you could say I'm his mentor.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.250
<i>Did a human shoot that arrow?</i>

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.880
What's your deal, anyway? You're strong.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.600
Where'd you learn that stunt?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.890
They teach you to swing poles
 in bridal training in Imihama?

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:59.980
I'm the captain of the Imihama 
Watch, Nekoyanagi Pawoo.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.860
Surrender and await your
 sentence, Mushroom Keeper.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.800
Next time, I'll split your skull.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.260
Aren't you supposed to tell people
 that <i>before</i> you go whacking them?

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.780
You look like you'd kill
 me even if I surrendered.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.420
Did I kill your parents or something?

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:14.670
I warned you!

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.800
<i>That's some awful Rusting she's got.</i>

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.240
<i>She can move like that even at death's door?</i>

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:36.320
I'd compliment your prowess 
in spite of all that Rusting,

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.690
but move too much and
 it'll hasten the spread.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:44.070
You say that without shame... after spreading 
the Rust to all the towns you've been through?!

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.820
Y'know, I'm sick of saying this,

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.280
but mushrooms don't spread the Rust!

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.320
Mushrooms...

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:54.800
...grow by consuming Rust.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.040
It's the only method we currently
 have of purifying the Rust.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.830
So it really is true.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.840
You don't look all that surprised.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.590
I guess that's a doctor for you,
 even if you are from the city.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.960
Don't overdo it! Any normal person
 with your wounds would've died.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:21.170
Lots of creatures have gone extinct
because of the Rust Wind.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:25.480
But life evolved to withstand the Wind.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:29.150
I always thought there had to be 
some organism in the outside world

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:33.100
that had adapted to the Rust in 
a way that it could thrive off of it.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:35.740
Your theory was correct.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:38.010
In short, that organism is...

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:38.990
...mushrooms.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:41.330
Utter nonsense.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:48.540
Who would ever believe
 something so preposterous?

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.970
If what you say is really true,

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.840
go and save Japan from 
the Rust Wind right now.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:58.650
I can't do that because of bastards like you!

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:02.720
How easily this gets misunderstood
 is a cause of great distress.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.190
Mushroom Keepers do grow mushrooms
 in places dense with Rust,

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.880
but they don't start purifying right away.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:14.860
So the casual observer just sees 
mushrooms growing where Rust is dense.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:19.090
So that's how the rumors that Mushroom
 Keepers spread the Rust started,

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:20.740
and why everyone persecutes them.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:23.510
Well, not much can be done about that.

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:26.300
Mushroom Keepers can't exactly socialize.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:31.630
And not all Mushroom Keepers
have good intentions, either.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:38.190
Some use their control of forbidden 
mushrooms in plots to amass fortunes—

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.640
I'm sorry! I pushed you too hard.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.820
Don't make an old timer talk so much.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.530
Imihama Watch Station

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:49.530
Vice Captain! The captain has engaged 
Akaboshi near the West Gate.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:52.020
All right, let's get over there, too.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.360
Looks like the special forces failed.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.190
Hmph.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:04.610
Well, if that woman from the Watch with 
the iron pole kills him, that's fine, too.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:07.160
Yap, yap, yap.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.920
I will not listen to the words of a villain!

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:36.850
Those two are monsters!

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:43.160
We just plant them to grow in places
we pass through that are dense with Rust.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.830
You should be grateful to us,

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:49.680
not trying to bash my head 
in with a weapon like that.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.930
You really think I'd believe
 a fairy tale like that?

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.210
You've covered every town 
you've been to in mushrooms,

00:08:56.210 --> 00:09:00.970
and your goal is to exact vengeance for the
 persecution of Mushroom Keepers, isn't it?

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.180
Wrong!

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.300
I'm looking for the Rust Eater.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.930
The Rust Eater?

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.310
Among Mushroom Keepers,

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:15.190
it is said to be a legendary mushroom 
born from the prayers of a dying hero.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:21.150
It's a mushroom that'll completely absorb even
 the deepest Rust, be it from man or machine.

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:24.710
I want to use it to save someone. 
That's why I've been traveling.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:27.330
So lower your pole and let me through.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.210
I have no business or grudge with Imihama.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:34.210
<b>Imi</b>

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:34.300
You think I'll be deceived
 by your stupid lies?

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:34.340
<b>Imi</b>

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.470
Prepare yourself, Akaboshi!

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:34.460
<b>Imi</b>

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.470
<b>Imi</b>

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:38.470
My pole will reach you were you stand!

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.580
<i>Why is Akaboshi so composed?</i>

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.970
<i>Is the sight of my Rusting upsetting him?</i>

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:48.980
<i>No, it doesn't matter what 
this Mushroom Keeper spouts.</i>

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.740
<i>Our next clash will end with me winning!</i>

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:55.620
Well, it's not like I haven't gained 
anything from coming to Imihama.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.890
You have a great doctor.

00:09:57.890 --> 00:09:59.350
He's taking care of us.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:01.550
His name's Nekoyanagi.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.250
You two are a lot alike.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.040
Do you know Milo?

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:07.990
Milo?

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.250
Did you do something to Milo?!

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.500
What did you do to Milo, you bastard?!

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:16.660
Did I do something to him, you ask?

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.270
<b>EAST</b>

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.020
<b>EAST</b>

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:45.560
m -27 11 l -46 4 l -46 12 l -27 19 l -27 11 

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:45.560
<b>Gunma</b>

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:49.550
I'd heard Mushroom Keepers can grow
 mushrooms even on barren land.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:51.410
I guess it was actually true.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:54.100
Dumbass. What the hell are 
you doing fawning over it?

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.670
It's common sense that 
mushroom spores spread Rust.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.450
If we don't do something 
about that giant mushroom,

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:03.400
this whole area will be 
covered in Rust in no time.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.400
Hey, bearded pig!

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:06.160
Huh?

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.140
Come on!

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:17.060
Give the King Trumpet your 
hippo dung once a week!

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.320
It won't grow as well with just sand!

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.090
Y-You want us to fertilize the mushroom?!

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:23.990
Listen closely, you pig bastard!

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:26.720
Mushrooms consume Rust to grow!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:34.010
I try to be nice, but seriously, 
every single one of them...

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:36.500
Why won't they just frickin' listen?!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.500
I'll remember your face, Akaboshi!

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.760
Next time, I'll rip out your tongue! You hear me?!

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:56.020
There's this nest of monsters called 
Weeping Child Ravine in Akita Prefecture.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:59.530
One of the Mushroom Keepers 
died there while hunting big game,

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:03.510
and when they went to bury him, 
they found it growing there.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:05.840
Weeping Child Ravine?

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.480
I feel dizzy.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:13.050
Jabi-san!

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:14.710
Jabi-san?!

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:17.280
So what if I did do something?

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:19.200
What do you think I did to him?

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:22.170
Don't you know what people call me?

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:34.930
You poisoned my iron pole?

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:39.410
If you hadn't stood around and 
listened to me talk, you would've won.

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:41.190
Akaboshi!

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:51.780
It wasn't a fair tactic, but it was hard 
for me to hit you since you're pretty.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:08.900
Milo...

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:27.860
Don't move.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:32.090
Put down the hostage and put your hands up.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:46.500
No mercy for a recovering old fart, huh?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.840
Jabi!

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.150
Y-You can move now? 
What happened to your wounds?!

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:57.900
See for yourself. I had 
six bullets in me, apparently.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.630
You damn geezer!

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:02.770
If you're gonna pull through, 
act healthier from the start!

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:06.210
Don't be dumb. I thought I was going to die.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:11.170
If it wasn't for that Panda brat's skill, 
it would've been the end of the line for me.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:12.340
He did this?

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:16.780
Though, you know, aren't I 
incredible for living through it, too?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.320
You dumbass! It's all because...

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:22.640
you made it sound like
 those were your last words.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:24.290
I...

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:26.120
J-Jabi-san!

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:29.550
What are you thinking, pretending
 to be dead in front of a doctor?!

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.640
I told you not to move around yet!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.550
Milo, you pulled it off?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.490
No, I only did what I could.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.810
That injection of yours worked.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:45.210
It's the way of the Mushroom Keepers
to repay their debts of gratitude.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.450
If there's anything I can 
do for you, name it.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:50.390
No, I only...

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:53.570
Pawoo!

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.010
So you two do know each other?

00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:59.130
Sh-She's my older sister.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:03.840
She was going all crazy earlier, 
so I shot her with some knockout poison.

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:04.950
She's just asleep.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.150
Knockout poison?

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.330
Akaboshi-san, you won?! Against Pawoo?!

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:13.390
Mushrooms will still be 
effective on her Rust.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.300
Use the stuff you gave to Jabi earlier.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:30.140
Incredible...

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:32.600
Bisco. This is no time to be spacing out.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:35.750
The Watch's iguana cavalry
 are closing in on us.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:39.920
It won't take 'em more than five minutes. 
Next time we're surrounded, we won't get away.

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:41.160
Got it.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.240
The North Gate's close. Let's go.

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:44.070
Yeah.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.640
I'll hold them off. You go on ahead.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:48.800
Sure.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:49.870
Wait, what?!

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:52.280
What do you mean, you'll hold them off?!

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.350
There's no point if you don't come with me!

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:56.260
Use your head, will ya?

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:01.380
There's no way an old man who just 
took six bullets can travel right away!

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:04.910
Use <i>your</i> head, old man! 
What about the synthesis?

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:08.910
Even if I harvest the Rust Eater, I need someone 
who can make it into medicine on the spot.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:10.900
Glance.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:12.930
Huh?

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:16.650
Have you gone senile, Jabi?

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:20.320
Akaboshi-san! Please take me with you!

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.950
The old man's been putting 
ideas in your head, hasn't he?!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:27.210
He told me about the Rust Eater. I can help you.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:30.720
I can synthesize medicine, 
and I can heal your wounds.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:32.300
Dumbass!

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:36.600
Who'd want to take you along? You're likely 
to die the moment I take my eyes off you!

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.590
You just said you'd grant any wish I had.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:41.970
I'm not some genie in a lamp.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:46.970
It's too dangerous outside the walls
 for a city brat like you to survive.

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:51.220
You'd be lucky to get off with losing 
one or both of those weak arms of yours.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.270
So what?

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:57.130
I might be able to save my sister, 
the only family I have.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.480
I'd gladly give my arms for that.

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:02.490
I don't even care if I lose my head!

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:17.510
Squads 2 and 3, fan out.
Loop around to the North Gate.

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.630
Bisco. It's the Watch.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.770
There's no more time for debating.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:30.270
If you don't wanna die, 
then listen to what I say.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:34.310
Mushroom Keepers fundamentally 
operate in pairs on journeys.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.820
If one dies, the other soon follows.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:37.780
Akaboshi-san!

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:42.160
Also! That right there. Stop with
 the pain-in-the-ass formality.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.870
Partners are always equals.

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:46.650
I'm Bisco.

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:48.100
You're Milo.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.240
Got it?

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:50.260
Yes, I underst—

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.250
Got it, Bisco.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.280
So a new tag team has been formed.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.260
We're positive they fled to this area!

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.760
Leave no stone unturned!

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:04.760
Found them!

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.780
Go. Get moving.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.770
Take care, Bisco.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.320
Hey!

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:25.280
Hey, what're you gonna do about
 your sister? Leave her sleeping?

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:29.410
She'll be fine. The guys in the 
Watch will take her into their care.

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:32.930
I put lots of those mushroom
 injections in her pouch, too.

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.370
Oh, but...

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:37.050
This might be the last time 
you ever see her, y'know.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.870
We don't have much time, 
but take one last good look at her.

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:44.190
You've protected me time after time.

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:46.600
You've been my shield.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:50.740
So just this one time, it's my
 turn to protect you, Pawoo,

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.480
and get hurt in your place.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:55.330
Okay?

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:58.490
I promise...

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.790
I promise I'll save you.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.600
So wait for me, Sis.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:09.250
I'm done, Bisco. I'm ready to go.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:13.240
Took you long enough, idiot!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.560
You wanna end our journey before it starts?!

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:19.760
<b>NORTH</b>

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:26.760
<b>Imi</b>

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:26.850
<b>Imi</b>

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:26.930
<b>Imi</b>

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:27.020
<b>Imi</b>

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:27.520
<b>Imi</b>

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.130
Run, Milo!

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:29.890
Right!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.700
There he is!

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:33.880
No, he's coming this way!

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.170
Does "Milo" mean what I think it does?

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:07.680
Yeah. Milo means " strong child." 
My mother gave it to me.

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:09.700
Not a bad name, then,

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:11.740
is it?!

00:22:09.570 --> 00:22:12.150
It's called the Nikko War Memorial.

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:16.900
Long ago, when they scrapped all 
the tanks and stuff that had rusted,

00:22:17.240 --> 00:22:20.420
they interred them in this
 temple and purified them.

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:24.530
That's why the torii are made 
from barrels that look like

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:26.390
the main gun off of something.

00:22:26.390 --> 00:22:29.660
What's that statue up on the roof?

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:31.490
The one with three monkeys lined up.

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:36.210
It's a sacred statue. The three wise monkeys: 
"See no evil, hear no evil, speak no evil."

00:22:36.590 --> 00:22:39.300
They're the three fast
 principles of the Watch.

00:22:39.600 --> 00:22:43.540
People say it was a statue of 
Tochigi's military regulations at the time.

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:46.550
Huh. You sure know a lot.

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:48.280
Well, I did go to school.

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:49.580
I see.

00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:52.560
Wait, who're you callin' 
bottom of the class?!

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:02.560
What incredible resilience.

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:05.570
Actagawa isn't a normal crab, either, is he?

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:21.710
The Nikko War Memorial...

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:23.350
is alive?!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:37.520
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:37.520
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:30.140
The destined pair start their 
journey and the tale finally begins,

00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:32.720
though the apocalyptic 
landscape isn't so forgiving.

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:35.640
It'd be a big help if they
 died at their next stop.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:37.500
Next episode: "Ride the Crab."

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:39.710
What does "ride the crab" even mean?

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Ride the Crab</b>
